.TH LALINFERENCE_NEST2POS "1" "January 2026" "LALInference" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lalinference_nest2pos \- lalinference_nest2pos.py takes at least one nested sampling output file and outputs posterior
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lalinference_nest2pos.py
[\fI\,-N Nlive\/\fR] [\fI\,-p posterior.hdf5\/\fR] [\fI\,-H header.txt\/\fR] [\fI\,--npos Npos\/\fR] [\fI\,--non-strict-versions\/\fR] \fI\,datafile1.hdf5 \/\fR[\fI\,datafile2.hdf5 \/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
lalinference_nest2pos.py takes at least one nested sampling output file and outputs posterior
.IP
samples. If more than one input file is specified, each file is converted,
then posterior samples drawn according to the evidence of each.
If the \fB\-\-npos\fR option is used the algorithm
will draw approximately that number of samples from the posterior. This may
give repeated samples in the output file. By default, the non\-repeating
algorithm is used, but that may not produce enough samples.
The input and output files may be in either HDF5 or ASCII format, with
ASCII tables being deprecated. The type will be chosen based on the file extensions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-N\fR NUM, \fB\-\-Nlive\fR=\fI\,NUM\/\fR
Number of live points in each chain loaded
.TP
\fB\-p\fR posterior.dat, \fB\-\-pos\fR=\fI\,posterior\/\fR.dat
Output file for posterior samples
.TP
\fB\-\-npos\fR=\fI\,NUM\/\fR
Draw a specific number of posteriors samples. May give
repetitions. Disabled by default.
.TP
\fB\-H\fR file.dat_params.txt, \fB\-\-headers\fR=\fI\,file\/\fR.dat_params.txt
Header file explaining columns in data file
.TP
\fB\-d\fR NUM, \fB\-\-prec\fR=\fI\,NUM\/\fR
Number of decimal place required for output posterior
samples. Default is 14.
.TP
\fB\-z\fR, \fB\-\-gzip\fR
Gzip compress the output posterior samples (this will
append .gz onto the posterior file). Default is no
compression.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print some additional information
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-strict\-versions\fR
Set this flag to allow combining of nested sample HDF5
files that do no necessarily have the same verion
information
